+	// ollama-metal: on macOS a DISCRETE GPU (e.g. AMD Radeon Pro W6800X on an
+	// Intel Mac Pro) is always a Metal device with NON-unified memory. With
+	// mmap on, llama.cpp wraps the mmap'd weight file in host-visible Metal
+	// buffers (MTL*_Mapped), so the GPU streams every weight over PCIe on each
+	// token -- crippling generation (measured: 1.6 t/s with mmap vs 61 t/s
+	// without on llama3.2). Disabling mmap makes the weights load into private
+	// VRAM. Apple Silicon GPUs are Integrated (UMA) so hasDiscreteGPU is false
+	// there and mmap stays on (free + saves memory). NOTE: gating here on goos
+	// rather than the Metal library string because on Intel macOS the device's
+	// DeviceID.Library carries the GPU name, not "Metal".
+	if goos == "darwin" && hasDiscreteGPU(gpus) {
+		return "metal_discrete"
+	}
